{
 "slug": "callout-table-footnotes",
 "module": "callout-table-footnotes/src/footnotes",
 "function": "scanFootnotes",
 "note": "args = [note text]; expected = numbers (id to number, in order of first reference, only ids with a definition), missing (referenced, no definition), unused (defined, never referenced), refs as [id, zero based line, zero based column of \"[\", context body|callout|quote|table], defs as [id, zero based line, definition text]. References in code spans, code blocks, front matter and after a backslash do not count. Reviewed by hand against each text. Inline footnotes on one line use an id with their line and column. Inline and named footnotes share one number order. Cases with function locateInline: args = [note text, named], expected = the marks of paragraph, list, task and blockquote footnotes as {id, kind, from, to, textFrom, text, number}; numbers come from the scanFootnotes counter, so callout and table footnotes count too. Code, math, comments, front matter, definitions, escaped carets and footnotes across a line break give no mark. Cases with function locateInlineLarge: the note is the lines of args[0] repeated args[1] times and joined with a newline; expected gives the mark count, the first and last number and the time limit in ms. A comment or math marker (%%, $$, <!--) whose closing marker does not come later in the note is plain text.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "one body reference",
   "args": [
    "A claim.[^1]\n\n[^1]: The source.\n"
   ],
   "expected": {
    "numbers": {
     "1": 1
    },
    "missing": [],
    "unused": [],
    "refs": [
     [
      "1",
      0,
      8,
      "body"
     ]
    ],
    "defs": [
     [
      "1",
      2,
      "The source."
     ]
    ]
   }
  },
  {
